I have a Jenkins pipeline that uses selenium to run tests on a web application. The pipeline is triggered by a pull request and a commit. The pipeline runs the tests and if any of the tests fail, it will fail the build. However, I would like to trigger the pipeline only if a specific test case fails. Is there a way to do this using selenium and Jenkins?
I have tried using the "Test Result Analyzer" plugin, but it only shows the results of the tests that were run, not the specific test case that failed. I have also tried using the "Junit" plugin, but it only shows the results of the tests that were run, not the specific test case that failed.
Is there a way to trigger the pipeline only if a specific test case fails using selenium and Jenkins?
Yes, you can use the "Test Result Analyzer" plugin to trigger the pipeline only if a specific test case fails. Here's how you can do it:

1. Install the "Test Result Analyzer" plugin in your Jenkins instance.
2. In your pipeline script, use the "testResult" step to run the tests and get the test results.
3. Use the "testResultAnalyzer" step to analyze the test results and get the specific test case that failed.
4. Use the "if" statement to check if the specific test case failed and trigger the pipeline only if it did.

Here's an example pipeline script that demonstrates how to use the "Test Result Analyzer" plugin to trigger the pipeline only if a specific test case fails:

```
pipeline {
    agent any

    stages {
        stage('Build') {
            steps {
                // Run the tests and get the test results
                testResult 'path/to/test/results.xml'
            }
        }
    }

    post {
        always {
            // Analyze the test results and get the specific test case that failed
            testResultAnalyzer 'path/to/test/results.xml'
        }
    }

    stage('Deploy') {
        steps {
            // Trigger the pipeline only if the specific test case failed
            if (testResultAnalyzer.getFailedTestCases().contains('specific.test.case')) {
                // Deploy the application
            }
        }
    }
}
```

In this example, the pipeline has two stages: "Build" and "Deploy". The "Build" stage runs the tests and gets the test results using the "testResult" step. The "Deploy" stage analyzes the test results using the "testResultAnalyzer" step and checks if the specific test case failed using the "if" statement. If the specific test case failed, the pipeline is triggered and the application is deployed.

Note that you'll need to replace "path/to/test/results.xml" with the actual path to your test results file. You'll also need to replace "specific.test.case" with the actual name of the test case that you want to trigger the pipeline for.</s>

